{"t": 1794109103.1835418, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "## Pipeline fix: `test:contract` failure on `main`\n\n**Root cause.** Pipeline [#8812](https://gitlab.com/acme/billing-legacy/-/pipelines/8812) (commit `a91c2e0`, `main`) fails in the `test:contract` job:\n\n```\ncontract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\nThe contract test encodes the Finance ERP import requirement (FIN-77): the sequence part of an invoice number must be zero-padded to six digits. `billing/invoice.py` interpolated the sequence as-is, so any sequence shorter than six digits produced an unpadded number (`INV-2026-42`), which the ERP import rejects.\n\n**Fix.** Format the sequence with a six-digit zero-padded field in `invoice_number()`:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nThe `INV-` prefix and the four-digit year are unchanged; only the sequence is padded. Verified against the contract assertion:\n\n```\n>>> invoice_number(2026, 42)\n'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\nThis is the formatting the ERP v2 switch in this MR needs, so the contract job should go green on `main` once this lands.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
